About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

Our Energy Products practice are looking for a Growth Marketing Executive to join the team. &nbsp;

Baringa's Energy Products business commercialises two decades of proprietary energy market expertise, data and models through a growing suite of subscription and SaaS products - from our Energy Insights platform (wholesale power, flexibility and energy attribute certificates across 60+ markets) to Energy Evaluate and our new AI-enabled tools. We are building and running this as a genuine products business, with a relentless focus on the customer, product-market fit, and the recurring revenue we retain and grow.

We are looking for a proactive hands-on Growth Marketing Executive to support marketing activity across our product, subscription, and software portfolio. This is an exciting opportunity for a motivated marketer looking to develop their career in product and growth marketing. &nbsp;

Reporting to the Energy Products Marketing Lead, and supporting the Marketing Manager, you will play a key role in campaign delivery, content creation, digital marketing, events and performance reporting, helping to drive awareness and demand across global markets. &nbsp;

What you will be doing

Campaign Support &nbsp;

• Support the planning and execution of integrated marketing campaigns. &nbsp;

• Coordinate campaign assets, timelines and stakeholder inputs. &nbsp;

• Assist with webinar, event, and product marketing activities. &nbsp;

• Help ensure campaigns are delivered on schedule and to a high standard. &nbsp;

Digital &amp; Growth Marketing &nbsp;

• Manage, create and optimise website content and landing pages. &nbsp;

• Support email marketing, social media and paid campaign activity. &nbsp;

• Conduct market research and competitor analysis. &nbsp;

• Identify opportunities to improve engagement and lead generation. &nbsp;

Content Creation &nbsp;

• Create and update marketing materials including webpages, email campaigns, blogs, presentations and social media content. &nbsp;

• Work with subject matter experts to translate technical content into engaging customer-focused communications. &nbsp;

• Support brand consistency across marketing materials. &nbsp;

Analytics &amp; Reporting &nbsp;

• Monitor campaign performance and marketing metrics. &nbsp;

• Produce regular performance reports and dashboards. &nbsp;

• Help identify insights and recommendations for future activity. &nbsp;

